			"notes": "## Hyperspace\n- Distortion Splicers can now be used during the Hoopa fight to escape, with a growing pull towards the way home.\n- Hoopa now waits 2 minutes instead of 10 seconds when nobody can battle it.\n- Sparkling Power now needs Sweet to be the donut's strongest flavour.\n- Fixed issues at the edges of Hyperspace islands.\n- Fixed distortions shrinking back after opening when the server lagged.\n\n## Wormholes\n- Removed the Big Battery. Pokémon can now target the Data Monitor: Electric moves charge it with a chance to break it, and other moves break it.\n- Celesteela and the Ultra Crater's giant Celesteela now need Complete Cobblemon Collection.\n\n## General\n- Added sound effects to Solgaleo, Lunala and Necrozma's signature moves.\n- Fixed selected moves being skipped after a boss phase.\n- Fixed 92 Pokémon cries that couldn't play.\n- Reduced the mod's download size from 77 MB to 48 MB.\n- Added commands: /hyperspace pity, /hyperspace bossCleared, /wormhole pity and /wormhole bossCleared.\n- Improved performance around distortions, island edges, minimap icons and the Ultra Plant.\n- Added configuration options, editable in Mod Menu or in config/hyperspace_wormholes_gameplay.json:\n  - Boss Pity\n  - Wormhole Base Shiny Chance and Multiplier Per Ring\n  - Donut Power strength\n  - Wormhole Ring quantity rarity\n  - Max distortions around per player\n  - Distortion star rating rarity\n  - Boss Hard Mode Always On\n  - Disable/Enable Data Monitor breaking per method of breaking"
		},
